From fb28c841fe96c2764800f46b4fceb4d4dd178440 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Wed, 30 Sep 2026 23:57:56 +0300
Subject: [PATCH] Comply with the licenses of everything the app ships

- Bundle demucs and julius without their dependencies: both declare torch, so the
  app build would otherwise include PyTorch and its CUDA libraries (several GB,
  under NVIDIA's license). einops and julius are listed in requirements.txt.
- Don't bundle imageio-ffmpeg: its FFmpeg binary is GPLv3. The app installs it
  from PyPI at first start, like PyTorch; a system ffmpeg is still preferred.
- Collect the license and notice files of every bundled package into licenses/
  in the app, and fail the build if a package has none (flatbuffers gets the
  Apache-2.0 text).
- Add the license texts of the libraries compiled into the bundled Python
  (python-build-standalone ships them only in its full archives).
- Update THIRD_PARTY_NOTICES.md (with the full license texts) and the README's
  License section for CDX23.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01HPyxjNMFEfFkn3iJrCGH7T
